{"name":"Otter Creek","hex":"#3f5a5d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Otter Creek","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A number of streams in the United States.","A town in Levy County, Florida."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Otter_Creek"}],"entries":[{"title":"Otter Creek (British Columbia)","blocks":[{"text":"Otter Creek is a creek located in the Atlin Country region of British Columbia. This creek flows into the south side of Lake Surprise about 2 miles west of Wright Creek. Otter Creek was discovered in 1898. The creek has been mined and for some years Compagnie Francaise des Mines d'Or du Canada hydraulicked a number of leases along Otter Creek."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Otter_Creek_(British_Columbia)","wikidata":"Q7109364"},{"title":"Mill Creek (Delaware River tributary)","blocks":[{"text":"Mill Creek is a 11.04 miles (17.77 km) long tributary of the Delaware River and is one of six streams in Bucks County, Pennsylvania by the same name. Mill Creek rises just east of Core Creek Park in Middletown Township and reaches its confluence at the Delaware River's 118.87 river mile in Bristol Borough."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mill_Creek_(Delaware_River_tributary)","wikidata":"Q38252028"},{"title":"Otter Creek (Vermont)","blocks":[{"text":"Otter Creek is the longest river entirely contained within the borders of Vermont. Roughly 112 miles (180 km) long, it is the primary watercourse running through Rutland County and Addison County. The mouth of the river flows into Lake Champlain."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Otter_creek_falls.jpg/330px-Otter_creek_falls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Otter_Creek_(Vermont)","wikidata":"Q1338233"},{"title":"Otter","blocks":[{"text":"Otters are carnivorous mammals in the subfamily Lutrinae. The 14 extant otter species are all semiaquatic, both freshwater and marine. Lutrinae is a branch of the Mustelidae family, which includes weasels, badgers, mink, and wolverines, among other animals."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Fischotter%2C_Lutra_Lutra.JPG/330px-Fischotter%2C_Lutra_Lutra.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Otter","wikidata":"Q200184"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/OtterCreekLoc.png/500px-OtterCreekLoc.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/OtterCreekLoc.png/500px-OtterCreekLoc.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOtterCreekLoc.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Otter_Creek_VT.jpg/500px-Otter_Creek_VT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Otter_Creek_VT.jpg/1280px-Otter_Creek_VT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Otter_Creek_VT.jpg/500px-Otter_Creek_VT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Otter Creek in Weybridge just north of the Lemon Fair River","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOtter_Creek_VT.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/August_2005_view_of_falls_on_Otter_Creek_from_Vergennes_town_dock.jpg/250px-August_2005_view_of_falls_on_Otter_Creek_from_Vergennes_town_dock.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/August_2005_view_of_falls_on_Otter_Creek_from_Vergennes_town_dock.jpg/500px-August_2005_view_of_fall